  annotation = {中文辅助译名：使用多分支共同注意循环网络进行电缆驱动手术机器人连续体关节的运动估计},
  abstract = {Minimally invasive flexible cable-driven surgical robots usually benefit from lower inertia, compact design, and remote actuation. Among the cable-driven surgical robots, the ones with continuum joints can adapt to complex cases through a high degree of dexterity and pliability. Nevertheless, this kind of robot poses challenges to accurate estimation of the joints’ motion, mainly due to the flexible deformation ability and the influence of uncertain cable extension, diverse surgical instruments, and collisions during surgery. Fortunately, the challenges can be addressed through learning on collected data, yet conventional data-driven methods fail to sufficiently consider the correlation between multiple estimation sources. To this end, we propose a data-driven approach of a multibranch coattention recurrent network (MCRN) for estimating the motion of a cable-driven surgical-robotic continuum joint, comprising a parallel 1-D-convolutional module, a multibranch coattention module, and a recurrent module. These three modules aim to achieve local description, cross-source fusion, and temporal description, respectively, for motion estimation based on multiple sources of input control signals and the force and torque series of the joint’s linkage. We perform experiments on the cable-driven continuum-joint motion estimation (CD-CJME) dataset, with the results showing that the proposed approach achieves better performance compared with conventional data-driven strategies for sequenti},
}

@misc{bjorn_schuller_c783b9e0b7494f64,
  title = {XAI-Grounded Explanation Generation for Speech Deepfake Detection with Training-Free Multimodal Large Language Models},
  author = {Berrak Sisman and Björn W. Schuller and Yupei Li and Xiaoliang Wu and Chenxi Wang and Qiyang Sun},
  year = {2026},
  doi = {10.21437/INTERSPEECH.2026-161},
